## Model card

- **Name:** LongCat 2.5 Preview
- **Short description:** Meituan's hosted-API preview of the LongCat 2 generation — released **2026-09-25** with a new image-understanding capability and "superior coding capability", served as an API-only preview (no open weights) at $0.30/$1.20 per 1M, plus a free OpenCode Zen slot. **Identity note:** the id in this folder (`opencode/longcat_2.5_preview`) matches no registry; the real ids are `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free` (Zen), `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (Vercel/NanoGPT canonical id) and `longcat-2.5-preview` (NanoGPT).
- **Provider / access:** LongCat API Platform (`https://api.longcat.chat`), Vercel AI Gateway (`meituan/longcat-2.5-preview`), NanoGPT, **OpenCode Zen `longcat-2.5-preview-free`** (free, limited time; the live Zen model list carries only that hyphenated id). Not on OpenRouter, not on Artificial Analysis, not on BenchLM.
- **Release / knowledge:** **2026-09-25** (LongCat platform change log). Knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (canonical), `longcat-2.5-preview` (NanoGPT), `longcat-2.5-preview-free` (Zen).
- **Context window:** **1,048,576** tokens; `max_tokens` limit **262,144** per LongCat's own parameter table (models.dev lists 131,072 for 2.5 and 262,144 for 2.0 — the two sources appear transposed; conflict flagged).
- **Modalities:** text and image input, text output; reasoning toggle; tool calling; temperature is fixed/overridden (not user-settable).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-20):** **$0.30/M in, $1.20/M out, $0.006/M cached read** ("Discounted Price, limited-time"; ¥2 / ¥8 / ¥0.04). Resellers list $0.30/$1.20 (Vercel) and $0.75/$2.95 (NanoGPT).
- **Architecture:** not published — no model card, no weights, no technical report, no parameter count. It is a hosted preview of the LongCat 2.0 generation (1.6T total / ~48B active MoE, MIT, 1M context), not a checkpoint anyone can inspect.

### Raw benchmarks found

> No benchmark row exists for LongCat-2.5-Preview on any source. The checks below are
> listed so the absence is auditable; the LongCat-2.0 numbers are a **different model**
> and are deliberately not used as a proxy.

- Artificial Analysis: no model page — `https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/longcat-2-5-preview` → **404** (verified live 2026-10-20)
- BenchLM: no model page — `https://benchlm.ai/models/longcat-2-5-preview` → **404** (verified live 2026-10-20)
- OpenRouter: `https://openrouter.ai/meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` → 404 (only `meituan/longcat-2.0` is listed)
- Hugging Face: no `LongCat-2.5*` repository exists (search returns 0); the `meituan-longcat` GitHub org's newest repos are LongCat-2.0 (2026-06-29) and LongCat-DeepResearch (2026-09-22)
- The platform change log claims "Superior Coding Capability" and multimodal understanding, but publishes **no numbers** for the preview
- Terminal-Bench / Tau2 / GDPval / GPQA / HLE / SWE-bench / LiveCodeBench / DeepSWE / MMMU-Pro / MRCR: **no verified public score found** for LongCat-2.5-Preview

### Negative findings summary

- No verified public benchmark, no third-party evaluation and no model card exist for this preview; only capability prose and a price table.
- No parameter count, architecture or weights are published.
- Closest **real** neighbouring model for orientation only (not used as a proxy): **LongCat 2.0** (MIT, 1.6T/48B active, 1M context) with its own card numbers — Terminal-Bench 2.1 70.8, SWE-bench Pro 59.5, GPQA-D 88.9, plus LongCat-DeepResearch (DeepResearchBench 55.25).

